rom. First is the horizontal bar chart or the vertical bar chart or the line chart, pie chart, donut chart and the funnel chart. The second Salesforce dashboard components is gauze. You can use a gauze when you have a single value that you want to show within a range of custom values. For example, if you want to show the revenue for a month, whether it was high, medium or low, you can show it with the help of goals. Third, we have metrics. You can use a metric when you have only one key value to display. For example, if you have a report showing the total number of particular products sold or is expected to be sold in the current month, you can name the value as a particular product selling target for the month and display it on the dashboard. The fourth Salesforce dashboard component is table. You can use a table to show a set of report data in column form. For example, if you want to see the top five selling product for your current month, you can do that using tables. The fifth Salesforce dashboard component is visual force page. You can use visual force page when you want to create a custom component or show information which is not available in another component type. So these were some of the Salesforce dashboard components. So now moving on to our next question. What is data skew? Data skew refers to a non-uniform distribution of the underlying data. This leads to stuck stages and task, low utilization of CPU and out of memory errors. This data skew is usually experienced while working for some big client with over 10,000 records. So there are three types of data skew. First one is the account data skew. This happens when too many child records are associated with the same parent object in one of the relationship. Then the imbalance would cause account data skew. The second type is ownership skew. This happens when a single user owns more than 10,000 records. Third, we have lookup skew. Lookup skew happens when there is a large number of records which are associated to a single record in the lookup object. So this was about data skew. Now let us move on to our next question. Our next question is explain skinny table and what are the consideration for skinny tables. So in Salesforce, skinny tables are used to access frequently used fields and avoid joints. The skinny tables have proved to improve performance significantly. Now how does it improve the performance? As we can see in the diagram here, for each object table that is visible to you, Salesforce maintains other separate table at the database level for the standard and custom fields. Now this operation is invisible to the customers and ordinary requires a join when a query contains both kind of fields. A skinny table contains both kind of fields and also omits soft deleted records or recycle bin records which helps speeding up the queries thus improving the performance. Some of the consideration for skinny tables would be skinny tables can contain a maximum of 100 columns. Next, skinny tables cannot contain fields from other objects. Also, skinny table don't include soft deleted rows such as recycle bin records. Next, you need to contact the Salesforce support to recreate tables or add new tables. So, now moving on to our next question. What is Apex? Well, Apex is a proprietary language developed by Salesforce.com. It is an object-oriented programming language that allows you to execute flow and transaction control statements on the force.com platform. One interesting fact about Apex is its syntax is 70% similar to Java. So, if you've worked on Java before, you can easily learn Apex. Then some of the functionalities of Apex would be you can add web and email services to your application or perform complex business processes. It can be used to add complex validation rules to your application and can also be used to add one or more custom logics. So now moving on to our next question. What are the different types of collections in Apex? So there are three main types of collection in Apex. The first is list. Now list is an order collection of element which is distinguished by the indexes. Now list elements can be of any data type. It could be primitive type, collection, userdefined types or built-in apex types. Next we have sets. Now sets is an unordered collection of element that do not contain any duplicates. Set elements can be of any data type. It could be primitive, collection, userdefined type or built-in apex type. And third we have maps. Now a map is a collection of key value pairs where each unique key maps to a single value. Now this keys and value can also be of any data type. Now I guess you have some idea about the different type of collection in Apex. So now let us move on to the next question and see what are getters and setter methods. Well the get method or the getter method is used to pass value from the controller to the visual force page whereas the set or the setter method is used to set the value back to the controller variable. Now look at the code snippet over here. Now here you can see we have used the get method to return the name which is to pass value to the visual force page and the set method is used to make the first letter of the name uppercase and the rest lower case. So now let us move on to our next question. Our next question is what do you mean by an interface in apex? So an interface is like an apex class in which none of the methods have been implemented. It only contains the method signature but the body of each method is empty. So to use an interface another class must implement it by providing a body for all the methods contained in that interface. Also all the interfaces in Apex are global and the methods in the interface are public and abstract methods. Moving on to next question. What is SOQL and what is it used for? Well SQL stands for Salesforce object query language. It is very similar to the widely used language SQL to query databases. But SQL is designed only for Salesforce data and is used to query the Salesforce platform to retrieve data. SQL can also be used with Apex and Visual Force to return sets of data. So this was about standard object query language. Now let us move on to our next question. Our next question is what is button overriding? While you can override the behavior of standard buttons like the new, view or edit in Salesforce classic, lightning experience and mobile independently. For example, you can also override the tab homepage that displays when a user clicks a standard, custom or external object tab. Now, moving on to our next question. What is the difference between a standard controller and a custom controller? Talking about the standard controller, first standard controller in Apex inherits all the standard object properties and the standard button functionalities directly. It contains the same functionality and logic that are used for standard Salesforce pages. Next, talking about custom controller. Custom controller in an Apex class implements all the logic for a page without levering a standard controller. Custom controllers are associated with visual force pages through the controller attribute. So this was the difference between standard controller and custom controller. So now let us move on to our next question. Our next question is what is who ID and what ID in activities? Well, who ID in Salesforce refers to people things. Example of who ID would be lead ID or a contact ID. Basically the who ID represents a human such as a contact or a lead. Next what ID in Salesforce refers to object type things. Example of what ID would be account ID or an opportunity ID. The W ID represents non-human objects such as accounts, opportunities, campaign cases or custom objects. So I guess you have some idea about what is who ID and what ID. So now let us move on to next question and see what is the use of an outbound message. An outbound message is nothing but an automation function that allows sending a message to external web services or an application when the record is created or updated in the Salesforce. These external web services can contain field values to introduce other processes in the external systems. Now outbound messages can be triggered by using workflow, approval process and entitlement process. So this was about outbound message. Now let us move on to next question. Our next question is how can you call a controller method from JavaScript? So to call a controller method that is an apex function from JavaScript, you need to use action function. This question can also be asked as what is the use of action function. So you can answer this by saying it is used to call a controller method from JavaScript. Now look at the piece of code here. Here you can see the function JS method call from any action calling the controller method from JavaScript. Moving on to the next question. What do you mean by batch Apex in Salesforce? Well actually batch Apex is used to run large jobs that would exceed normal processing limits. Using batch Apex you can process record asynchronously in batches to stay with platform limits. So now to process every query separately it will take you a lot of time. So batch Apex allows the breaking of a single job into flexible batches. So let's say you have 10,000 plus records you have to execute. So instead of executing all of them at once, you can batch the records for example a batch of 200 and then processes 200 records at one time. Then after that you can move on to the next 200 and so on. So I guess you have understood what exactly is batch Apex in Salesforce. So now let us move on to the next question and see what are the methods to implement batch apex. So in order to use the batch apex you need to write apex class that implements database batchable interface and make your class global. Next you have to implement the following three methods. The first one is the start method. This method is called once at the beginning of the batch apex job and is used to collect the records or object to be passed to the interface method. The next method is the execute method. Execute method performs an operation which we want to perform on the records fetch from the start method and last we have the finish method. Now this finish method executes after all the batches are processed and is used to send confirmation email notification. You can see the syntax for all start method, execute method and the finish method. So I guess you have some idea about what are the methods to implement batch apex. So now let us move on to our next question and see what are the difference between SQL and SOSL. Well, we have discussed about SOQL in question number 33. So I guess you have some idea about it by now. So let us talk about Salesforce object search language or SOSL first. SOSL is a Salesforce search language that is used to perform text searches in records. Now talking about some of the differences between them. The first difference would be SQL returns record while SOSL returns fields. Next, SQL uses select keyword for the retrieval of record from the databases whereas SOSL uses find keyword for retrieval of record from databases. The third differences is in SOQL only one object can be searched at one time whereas in SOSL many objects can be searched at one time. Next in SOQL one can query any type of field but in SOSL one can query only email text or phone number. So these were some of the major difference between SQL and SOSL. So now moving on to our next question. Is it possible to edit Apex class or triggers in the production environment? Well the answer for this is no it is not possible. We cannot directly edit the Apex class or trigger in the production environment. It can only be done in the developer edition sandbox or or the testing or moving on to the next question. What is apex trigger? Now apex trigger performs custom action to the record in Salesforce before or after the events. Examples of such actions include insertion, updation or deletion of records in Salesforce. The trigger help in performing operation that are subjected to specific condition such as modifying related records or restricting certain operations. Triggers can be used for anything you do in Apex, executing SQL or data manipulating language or even calling custom Apex methods. So there are two different types of triggers in Salesforce. The first one is before trigger and the second one is after trigger. before trigger is executed to validate the record values before saving to the database whereas the after trigger is executed to validate the record values after saving the database. Now I guess you have some idea about what is apex trigger. So let us move on to our next question. Our next question is how can you call an apex class in Salesforce? Well, we can call an Apex class in Salesforce from the following ways. The first one is from the visual force page or from the developer console. We can also call the Apex class from the JavaScript links or by using a trigger. Next, you can call a Apex class from another class or from homepage components. So these are the various ways you can call an Apex class in Salesforce. So this brings us to our next question. If required, can two users share the same profile? Well, the simple answer for this would be yes. In Salesforce, it is possible to assign a similar profile to different people or teams or managers. The advantage of this would be at the same time the entire team or the group of people can hold access to crucial data. So for example the HR team named the HR profile can have access to candidates, employees, lead data and all the information they need. So these were some of the important and frequently asked Salesforce interview question and answers. Now let us move on to our next topic and see some of the tips to become a Salesforce developer. Before we start this, I would like to say there is no such prerequisites to become a Salesforce developer. But companies 